nds.\n7. **Commented-Out Corpse** (L33–37): a disabled legacy-refund snippet sitting immediately above the live function. Easy to mistake for intended behaviour.\n8. **God File**: 310 lines, just over the 300 threshold.\n9. **String Sprinkles**: `\"enterprise\"` duplicated across four production files (`api/plan.ts`, `billing.ts:7`, `jobs/plan-sync.ts`, `ui/pricing.ts`).\n\n**Low**\n10. **Catch and Release** (L245–247): the email retry loop's `catch` has no binding and only a comment — the caller is told the invoice succeeded whether or not the email did.\n11. **Unfinished Business**: 4 markers (FIXME/HACK/XXX/TODO) at L183–308, including \"should not log full PII in production.\"\n\n## One thing the report surfaces that's easy to miss\n\n`clues.suppressions` shows a pin on `commented_out_code::src/billing.ts::` with `matches_current_finding: false`. The repo scan explains why: the fingerprint format changed in schema 0.8.0, so the pin lapsed and finding #7 is live again with nothing silencing it. The suppression's stated reason (\"kept for one more release; will be deleted in v0.3\") suggests deletion was already the agreed outcome — a deliberate decision that quietly stopped applying, not one that was reversed.\n\nTwo duplications the detectors didn't flag as such but which matter for any edit: the tax ladder exists twice (L145 inline vs `tax()` at L257), and the loyalty/age discount at L91 duplicates `recommendUpgrade`'s tenure logic. Changing a rate or a tenure threshold in one place silently leaves the other stale.",
